load @term/seed/type/self
  find self-type

# The natural numbers, the first counting structure, encoded as a self type carrying its induction principle, in the
# same shape as the booleans. The two constructors are zero and successor, and the induction principle says a predicate
# holding at zero and across successor holds for every natural. Counting the distinctions gives the naturals, and
# ordering them, then signing them, gives the integers, the unique totally ordered rung whose one-way order is the
# arrow of time. This is the first object the theory rests on.
#
# The rules. Introduction: zero inhabits the natural, and the successor of a natural is a natural. Elimination
# (induction): to prove a predicate for every natural, prove it at zero and prove it carries from a natural to its
# successor. Computation: the eliminator at zero yields the zero case, and at a successor yields the step applied to
# the predecessor's result. The arithmetic (addition as repeated successor, multiplication as repeated addition) and
# the order are developed, with machine-checked proofs, in the number files.
form natural-type
  link encoding, like self-type
